cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "anchorgate: an evaluation protocol with a gate for spatiotemporal predictions"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-07
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ninja-marduk/anchorgate"
authors:
  - family-names: "Perez Reyes"
    given-names: "Manuel Ricardo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-2963-1631"
    affiliation: "Pedagogical and Technological University of Colombia (UPTC)"
abstract: >
  anchorgate scores saved predictions of a spatiotemporal field against untrained references
  (per-cell climatology, persistence, seasonal naive) on identical targets, audits whether a
  cross-validation assignment is out of sample given the forecast horizon, resolves seed
  variance before any architectural claim, and refuses conclusions the computations do not
  support. Every report carries the hash of a declaration written before scoring.
